## 4.2 Automatic Case Creation

When a valid inquiry is received:

1. Validate the request.
2. Check the idempotency key.
3. Create a unique case identifier.
4. Assign initial status New.
5. Record the submission timestamp.
6. Store the selected service domain.
7. Store the selected target timeline.
8. Create an initial status-history event.
9. Record the intake event in the activity log.
10. Create an administrator notification.
11. Return a tracking reference to the requester.
12. Update dashboard data through the supported refresh mechanism.

The database transaction must not create a partial case when an essential operation fails.

Do not generate duplicate cases from repeated requests using the same idempotency key.

Case numbers must be unique and safe under concurrent submissions.

## 4.3 Case Status Rules

